---
import { href } from '../../i18n';
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Soul Matcha handles the information of people who visit this site."
  updated="October 15, 2026"
  routeKey="privacy"
>
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    This site is informational. We do not collect personal data: there are no
    forms, user accounts, purchases or comments.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not use analytics or measurement tools.</li>
    <li>We do not use advertising or tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>
      We do not embed third-party content, such as maps, videos or social media
      buttons.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do not load resources from other domains: fonts and images are served
      from this same site.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical data from hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. As with any web server, the host may
    log technical data about each visit (for example, the IP address, browser
    and date) for security and operational purposes. We do not access or use
    those logs. To see how they are handled, read the host's{' '}
    <a
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      GitHub privacy statement
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <p>If we change hosting provider, we will update this notice.</p>

  <h2>Storage in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The site stores a few technical items in your browser in order to work. They
    contain no personal information. See the details on the{' '}
    <a href={href('cookies', 'en')}>cookies page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    When we add links to social media or other sites, those will have their own
    privacy policies, separate from this notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    If the site starts to collect data (for example, with a contact form or
    analytics), we will update this notice beforehand and, where applicable, ask
    for your consent.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller and contact</h2>
  <p class="pending">
    Pending: name or legal entity of the controller and a contact method (for
    example, an email address).
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
